		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  [9.3] nommer les récursions d'une requête récursive]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=19985#p19985"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Et voilà la réponse :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>WITH RECURSIVE en_aval(profondeur, code_zone, id_nd_ini, id_nd_fin, geom) AS (
SELECT  MAX(code_zone) OVER () AS  profondeur, code_zone, id_nd_ini, id_nd_fin, geom FROM essai_pl
    UNION ALL
        SELECT  MAX(e.code_zone)  OVER () AS  profondeur, e.code_zone, e.id_nd_ini, e.id_nd_fin, e.geom
        FROM    en_aval  AS ea
        INNER JOIN essai_pl AS e 
        ON  e.id_nd_fin = ea.id_nd_ini)
SELECT  ROW_NUMBER() OVER()::integer AS gid, profondeur, code_zone, id_nd_ini, id_nd_fin, geom FROM en_aval;</code></pre></div><p>Bon week-end !</p>]]></content>
